{
  "_comment": "Config for the /server slash commands + watchdog. Public IDs only, no secrets. owner_ids = Discord user IDs that may start/stop/restart (in addition to guild admins); empty [] means 'guild admins only'. Get your ID: Discord Settings > Advanced > Developer Mode ON, then right-click your name > Copy User ID. servers: key = exaroton server ID; watch=true means the watchdog alerts on its crash/up/down; auto_stop_empty stops it after empty_grace_seconds with no players. auto_reply_guilds = guild IDs where the autonomous voice brain (BENHAM_AUTO_REPLY=1) may self-reply; omit or set to just your test guild so Benham never auto-replies in friend servers. command_guilds = which Discord guilds get the /server slash commands and WHICH exaroton servers each may control (a server whitelist per Discord guild): key = guild ID, servers = \"*\" for all or a list of exaroton server IDs, require_operator = true means start/stop/restart still need an operator (owner_ids or a guild admin), false means anyone in that guild may control the whitelisted servers.",
